$chapters = [
    my_ch('1. InnoDB Architecture, Collations & Data Types', 'MySQL 8 Architecture & InnoDB Storage Engine (Clustered PK & Buffer Pool)', 'mysql 8 architecture, innodb vs myisam, innodb clustered index, innodb_buffer_pool_size',
        '**MySQL 8** powers the majority of transactional web applications worldwide using **InnoDB**—an ACID-compliant, row-locking storage engine where **the table itself IS physically organized on disk as the Primary Key B+Tree (Clustered Index)**!',
        ['**Why Primary Key Size Impacts EVERY Secondary Index in InnoDB!**: Unlike PostgreSQL (where secondary indexes point to physical heap `ctid`s), **every InnoDB secondary index leaf stores a copy of the row\'s Primary Key**! Using a bulky `VARCHAR(100)` as a Primary Key bloats *all 6 secondary indexes* on that table and requires two B+Tree lookups on non-covering reads!', '**`innodb_buffer_pool_size`**: Caches 16KB data and index pages in RAM—size to **70%–80% of server RAM** on dedicated DB hosts.', '**Removed Query Cache in MySQL 8**: MySQL 5.7\'s mutex-bottlenecked Query Cache was permanently removed in MySQL 8.0—use Redis/ProxySQL for application caching.'],
        [['`Clustered Index (PK)`', '16KB B+Tree leaf pages contain the entire row', 'Sequential `BIGINT UNSIGNED AUTO_INCREMENT` appends cleanly at the right edge without page splits!'], ['`Secondary Index`', 'Leaf stores `(indexed_cols, PK_value)`', 'If all `SELECT`ed columns are in `(indexed_cols, PK)`, MySQL skips the second PK lookup (`Using index` covering scan)!'], ['`Redo Log + Doublewrite Buffer`', 'Crash-safe torn-page & ACID recovery', 'Guarantees zero corrupted 16KB pages on sudden OS power loss.']],
        "SELECT VERSION() AS mysql_version, DATABASE() AS active_schema;",
